{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/784304-non-european-nobles","id":784304,"title":"Non European Nobles!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-11T12:49:59-08:00","id":784304,"title":"Non European Nobles!","content":"Frankly, it is kind of iffy that the only Nobles are the very European Sidhe. No the Eshu Nobles don't quiet cut it. We need non-Wester groups of Nobles. The Chinese Nobles in the Land of 8 Million Dreams were a start. Lets get them in a players book and some Djinni and Peris too. Do you know of any Fay myths that would make good non-European Nobles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T13:05:35-08:00","id":784313,"title":"","content":"The Menehune's <i>ali'i</i> are another group of canon nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T14:38:56-08:00","id":784358,"title":"","content":"The Oba and ali'i should have corebook coverage, really, even if they're just subkiths listed under the main splat DPSs. That'll go some way to addressing the 'gorgeous Aryan/Celtic masters with divine right to rule every other race' thing (not always true, but about as popular a motif as the Assamite 'Saracen'). It's a bit icky as is. But I know Black Hat Matt is supposed to be doing more to address the presentation of the sidhe, so I'm sure he's considered this.<br /> <br /> There should be some Greek or non-Celtic European nobles too, plus some Indian Subcontinent nobles and some for other ethnic/cultural groups. But, luckily, the 10K stretch goal on creating your own kith will help in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T20:44:35-08:00","id":784518,"title":"","content":"From what I am to understand Oba covered Africa, India-subcontinent, and the Middle East. The Kami of the Hisen covered the Far East. Various Nunnehi Kiths were nobility of Pacific islands, Caribbean islands and The Americas. Australia has always been a mystery in Changeling, the assumption from what little is sprinkled throughout the editions is that Eshu and Nunnehi share Australia? The Sidhe are nobility of European origin. They rule in North America only because of setting conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T21:35:50-08:00","id":784528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/784304-non-european-nobles?p=784358#post784358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be some Greek or non-Celtic European nobles too, plus some Indian Subcontinent nobles and some for other ethnic/cultural groups. But, luckily, the 10K stretch goal on creating your own kith will help in this regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see some Indian Kiths in general much less Nobles.. and no Oba don't count, they are no more indian Nobles than Sidhe are and have as much cultural connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T00:49:22-08:00","id":784590,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always thought it was a bit of a cop-out to have Eshu as the 'Orientalist' kith. Eshu is an African god, so has very little to do with India and the Middle East. Now Eshu in the Caribbean I could understand, but the books always explicitly said Oba can only come from the kith's ancestral lands, which makes playing Caribbean Oba impossible. <br /> <br /> If new kiths were created with new diasporic cultures (because those cultures tend to be only a few hundred years old but have very distinct cultures of their own), in theory you could have some very cool Caribbean kiths based on, say, duppies, jumbies, lagahoo, La Diablesse, soucouyant, etc. As the indigenous populations of the Caribbean (Tainos, Arawaks, etc) were mostly wiped out by the settlers, and only sometimes interbred with the newcomers, you'd potentially have a select few Nunnehi surrounded in their ancestral lands by new kiths of West African, Indian, Chinese and European origin. That could be pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> Damn, I wanna write a Caribbean book now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T09:33:39-08:00","id":784804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/784304-non-european-nobles?p=784518#post784518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Australia has always been a mystery in Changeling, the assumption from what little is sprinkled throughout the editions is that Eshu and Nunnehi share Australia? The Sidhe are nobility of European origin. They rule in North America only because of setting conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of the late Changeling books &quot;Fool's Luck&quot; they described Australia's changelings as much like Concordia's only more peaceful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T09:35:36-08:00","id":784805,"title":"","content":"Getting the Djinni as an official set of Kith's which would logically include Noble Djinnis, would cover vast areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}